<PublicPageLayout current="data-sources" eyebrow="Traceable by design" title="Data sources" description="Scrooner prioritizes primary, public sources and keeps the path back to original disclosures visible wherever practical.">
  <section>
    <h2>Primary source</h2>
    <h3>SEC EDGAR</h3>
    <p>Company financial facts, filing history, and related disclosure data originate from filings and structured data made available through the US Securities and Exchange Commission’s EDGAR system.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Search SEC EDGAR <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="ds-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>How to read the data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Periods and filing dates matter: the latest filing may include restated prior periods.</li>
      <li>Not every company reports every concept in the same form.</li>
      <li>Derived ratios depend on the availability and consistency of their input facts.</li>
      <li>Market and ownership data can have different update schedules from financial statements.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="public-callout">
    <h2>Source questions</h2>
    <p>When a value looks surprising, use the company page’s filing context and compare it with the original filing. Scrooner’s purpose is to make that verification easier, not to obscure it.</p>
  </section>
</PublicPageLayout>
